{
  "requirement": "If the accepted result cannot be deserialized into `R`, awaiting the builder\nreturns `ValidationError::Agent`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligation.** `judge.submission.decoding` has one obligation. If the harness's accepted result cannot be deserialized into `R`, awaiting the builder returns `ValidationError::Agent`.\n\n**Implementation path, read only to see how the test reaches the requirement.**\n- `GraphSession::submit` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tools.rs` accepts any argument object of the form `{result: <any value>}`. It does this through `submitted_value`.\n- Deserializing into `R` happens afterwards in `Ask::execute` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/procedure.rs`. It calls `serde_json::from_value(value)` and maps the failure to `ValidationError::Agent`.\n- So a well-formed submission with a wrong-typed `result` is accepted by the harness and then fails decoding. That is exactly the case the requirement describes.\n\n**Test mapping.** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs#fn[typed_submission_references_resolve_and_invalid_results_are_agent_errors]` carries a `{test}` reference to the subject.\n- **Decoding failure.** The first loop case submits `{\"result\":\"wrong\"}` and calls `ctx.ask::<bool>()`. The harness accepts the string, deserialization into `bool` fails, and the test asserts `Err(ValidationError::Agent(_))`. This is the required failure scenario and outcome.\n- **Success contrast.** The same test first submits `{\"result\":{\"decision\":\"Yes\"}}` for `ask::<Answer>()`. It asserts the decoded `Decision::Yes`, so the Agent error is not returned unconditionally.\n- **Extra malformed submissions.** The missing `result`, wrong key and extra key cases also assert `ValidationError::Agent`. Those are harness-level rejections that fall under the harness requirements, but they do no harm here.\n\n**Other coverage.** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/validation.rs#fn[invalid_typed_submission_is_an_agent_error]` also checks that an invalid typed submission gives `ValidationError::Agent`. That holds both for `ctx.ask::<Answer>()` and through `Validator::verify`. It is marked for `judge.submission`, not for this subject, but it supports the same behavior.\n\n**Gaps.** I found none. The requirement has a single failure condition and a single required error variant. The test exercises that condition and asserts the variant.",
